# Repository-wide line-ending policy.
#
# Store every text file with LF in the repository and check it out with LF on
# every platform. `text=auto` lets git detect binary files and leave them byte
# for byte; `eol=lf` forces LF for everything it treats as text. This ends the
# mixed CRLF/LF state that made the pre-commit line-ending fixer rewrite whole
# files whenever they were touched.
#
# Per-directory .gitattributes (src/Mod, src/Doc, ...) still apply on top of
# this baseline; they only set the `text` attribute, so the `eol=lf` here still
# governs their checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored / third-party sources keep their upstream line endings so our copies
# do not diverge from upstream and create needless conflicts on dependency
# updates.
src/3rdParty/** -text
tests/lib/**    -text
